{"repositoryId":842385453,"availability":"available","full":"marinasundstrom/raven","name":"raven","description":"Raven is a pragmatic, typed, general-purpose programming language for .NET.","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":112,"forks":1,"created":"2024-08-14T08:41:34Z","updated":"2026-10-16T18:34:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://marinasundstrom.github.io/raven/","topics":["compiler","compiler-construction","csharp","dotnet","roslyn"],"demo":"https://marinasundstrom.github.io/raven/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.659Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.659Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.659Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.659Z","stars":112,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Raven is a pragmatic, typed, general-purpose programming language for .NET. It makes functional composition, algebraic modeling, procedural code, and object-oriented design complementary parts of one toolset, with direct access to the .NET runtime and ecosystem.","Raven is under active development. Its language and compiler combine an expression-oriented surface, explicit mutability, structural pattern matching, Option/Result-based flow, and direct interoperability with existing .NET libraries.","Raven is not defined by a single programming paradigm. It provides syntax, types, and libraries for functional programming patterns where transformations and data flow benefit from them, while retaining first-class procedural, object-oriented, and systems-oriented programming tools."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marinasundstrom/raven/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6acea978431d20cf98fa53671c45b309ce3279832434f9ea5c76a87f90206bb5","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.821Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:00:48.821Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Raven is a pragmatic, typed, general-purpose programming lang